        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Getting Set Up\n",
        "For this activity, you will pair program: two people sharing one keyboard. The handout for this activity has reminders about the two roles.\n",
        "\n",
        "To start, the person whose first name comes later in the alphabet should be the Computer, and the person whose name comes earlier in the alphabet should be the Navigator.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Exploring Variables\n",
        "\n",
        "Choose two of the remaining numerical variables in the dataset to investigate their relationship to `price`. The options are: `bed`, `bath`, `year_built`, and `lot`.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "What two variables did you choose?\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "You'll make graphs and calculate correlations to see how each of those variables might be related to `price`. Start by making a scatterplot with **one** of your chosen variables as the explanatory variable (x) and `price` as the response variable (y).\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank1\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: price\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank2\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank3\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank4\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "ggplot(duke_forest) +\n",
        "  aes(x = blank1, y = price) +\n",
        "  geom_point() + \n",
        "  labs(\n",
        "    title = \"blank2\",\n",
        "    x = \"blank3\",\n",
        "    y = \"blank4\"\n",
        "  )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "Describe the relationship in the scatterplot. Is it linear or nonlinear? Strong, moderate, or weak? If it is linear, is it positive or negative?\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "To get a quantitative sense of the relationship, calculate the correlation between your first variable and `price`.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank1\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: price\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "cor(duke_forest$blank1, duke_forest$price, \"pairwise.complete.obs\")\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "Is the value of the correlation what you expected based on the scatterplot? Why or why not?\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Now do the same with your other variable. First, the scatterplot.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank1\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: price\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
