        "\n",
        "## Simple Linear Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "**Before starting this section,** switch who is the Computer and who is the Navigator.\n",
        "\n",
        "Now you'll use the variable you chose at the end of the last section to make a linear regression model for predicting `price`. Fill in the blanks below to make a model with your variable as the explanatory variable and `price` as the response variable.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank1\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: price\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "model1 <- lm(price ~ blank1, duke_forest)\n",
        "summary(model1)\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "What is the equation of the regression line from this model?\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "Choose an example value of your explanatory variable. Say that value, and use your model to predict what the price of that house would be.\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "You can also add your regression line into the scatterplot using `geom_smooth()`. Fill in the blanks below.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks}\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank1\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: price\n",
        "#|   prefill: true\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank2\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank3\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "#| blank:\n",
        "#|   target: blank4\n",
        "#|   prefill: false\n",
        "#|   occurrence: 1\n",
        "#|   match: token\n",
        "\n",
        "ggplot(duke_forest) +\n",
        "  aes(x = blank1, y = price) +\n",
        "  geom_point() + \n",
        "  geom_smooth(method = lm, se = FALSE) +\n",
        "  labs(\n",
        "    title = \"blank2\",\n",
        "    x = \"blank3\",\n",
        "    y = \"blank4\"\n",
        "  )\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "How strong of a fit does the model visually seem to be to the data?\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "**STOP.** Check in with Aidan or Dr. O here.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{code-blanks-response}\n",
        "Find the \"Multiple R-squared\" in the linear regression output. What is this value? Is this what you would expect visually from the scatterplot and regression line, and why or why not?\n",
        "```\n",
